WEBVTT

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:08.240
It's beautiful.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.480
Yeah!

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.910
We are passing by a large lake.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:15.600
This lake is said to have 
been built by beavers.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.040
Wow!

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:22.250
Trees flourish in this area because of
the moderately warm temperatures.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:30.800
The view is gorgeous, as well. 
Perfect for a drive.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.890
Come to think of it, how does the bus move?

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:38.180
Lucky-san, you're not touching it, right?

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:42.460
It is semi-automatically driving 
through a wireless link with me.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:45.190
It can also be driven manually.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:46.690
Wow.

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:51.250
Would you like to try? 
The steering wheel is here.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.450
Um... No, thanks.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.740
Meow! I wanna try!

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:02.620
Boss, I just have to move this, right?

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.170
This is fun!

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:17.410
Do you know what you're doing, Serval-chan?

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.200
Don't worry!

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.100
Oh, what's this thing by my feet?

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:23.180
I-I-I... I'm sorry...

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:25.350
Nah, it's okay.

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:29.410
I hadn't built it yet anyway, 
so don't worry about it.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:34.440
I'm American Beaver, but you can 
call me Beaver. Nice to meetcha.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:34.980
Order: Rodentia
Family: Castoridae
Genus: Castor

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:38.590
I'm Serval! And this is Kaban-chan.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:40.490
It's very nice to meet you.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:41.570
Kaban?

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:44.220
Were you trying to build something?

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:47.950
Yup, this is what I want to build.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.270
Do you know what this is?

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.870
What an odd shape.

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:57.340
Are those trees?

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:02.770
I think it's a house. It's so awesome.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:08.700
I think you have to put 
trees together, like this.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:12.980
Wow! You can tell how to build 
it just from looking at this?

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:16.860
That's right. I guess I'm good at building.

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:22.520
So I thought maybe I could build it 
myself and gathered the materials...

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:25.890
But when I was just about to get started,

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:30.040
and the materials were suddenly 
in front of me, I got anxious.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.750
I couldn't make up my mind.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:36.370
The next thing I knew, 
a few days had passed...

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:39.000
Gnaw, gnaw, gnaw, gnaw...

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:38.430
Are you a worrywart?

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.910
It's okay. You can do it, Beaver!

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:43.200
That's right.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:47.590
It's amazing that you can understand 
how something's made just by seeing it.

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:49.770
Y-You think so?

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:53.810
It's not so easy to get a hold 
of the materials, though...

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:55.770
Huh?

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:59.720
By the way, did I thank you for that tree?

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:04.130
I have to give the professor three 
months' worth of Japari buns.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:07.240
I already gave away the last house...

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:09.210
It's just not possible.

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:12.040
I'm sorry! Wait!

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:16.460
Leave this to us. We'll get 
new materials for you!

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:19.690
Where can we get materials?

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:25.860
This area is a "mixed forest." They are 
composed of multiple kinds of trees.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:30.510
For building materials, I would 
recommend straight conifers.

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:35.060
There is an ideal grove a short drive away.

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:37.840
Got it. Let's go!

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:40.920
Beaver, come with us. 
It'll be a nice diversion!

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:42.460
Gotcha!

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:51.450
Now, off we go.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.240
Yeah!

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:55.160
Wait a minute!

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:56.370
What is it?

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:59.690
I've got this... Am I forgetting anything?

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:02.210
Nope. Okay, I'm ready!

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:02.820
Then...

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:03.830
Wait!

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:07.710
My dam doesn't have any holes, right?

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:10.400
It's okay to leave it for a little while, right?

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.350
You're overthinking this!

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:20.020
Wow, this is really incredible.

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:22.870
Right? It's called the Japari Bus!

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:24.590
We all fixed it together.

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:29.950
It's like a moving house. 
This is pretty awesome, too.

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:31.210
Right? Right?

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:35.450
Although I crashed into your trees with it...

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:41.080
Please look at the tree to the upper right.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:43.610
That is a long-tailed tit's nest.

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:48.550
They build their nests out 
of lichen and cobwebs.

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:54.510
Its color and shape, resembling a tree knot, 
camouflages the nest from predators.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:58.230
Next, please look to our left.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.240
This is a megapode nest.

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:07.270
The males use dirt and fallen leaves 
to build a mound in which

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:09.780
the female lays her eggs.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:12.390
Everyone's so amazing.

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:15.710
I'd end up just taking a nap wherever.

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:19.850
I get anxious when I'm too out in the open.

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:23.460
It seems that there are some 
Friends who make homes as

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:26.340
a behavior carried over from 
when they were animals.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:33.090
Because their bodies become so different, 
it is very difficult at first.

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:35.180
It was like that for me, too.

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:38.770
I'd rather have a smaller house,

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:41.990
but with a body like this, it has to be big.

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:46.260
I can relate. Small spaces are calming.

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:50.690
Yeah, exactly. And you can make 
coverings so no one can see inside!

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:54.560
That sounds nice and calming!

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:57.230
You two might be pretty alike.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:59.290
It's within sight now.

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:05.620
Wow, there are so many straight trees!

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:08.210
They look like pretty good materials.

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:12.090
Wow...

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:16.940
Are you okay, Serval-chan?

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:18.560
What happened?

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:21.690
I'm okay.

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:24.600
The ground here is really something, huh?

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.180
It's full of holes!

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:31.630
Does something live here?

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:33.090
Huh?

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:39.940
What are you doing?

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:41.870
Are you okay?

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:56.340
What do you think you're doing? 
I'll bury you alive!

00:08:56.650 --> 00:09:00.060
Huh? She doesn't mean us, right?

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.460
I think she buried herself.

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:03.190
Huh?

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:08.900
You saved me? Thank you!

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:12.240
I was sure someone had 
tried to bury me alive.

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:14.190
We'd never do something so terrible!

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:20.160
Order: Rodentia
Family: Sciuridae
Genus: Cynomys

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:20.160
Hello. I'm Prairie Dog. 
Please allow me to greet you.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:21.800
It's nice to meet you.

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:22.870
Hiya.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.850
Huh?!

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:34.470
That is a greeting in the prairie tradition.

00:09:43.700 --> 00:10:13.270
Tobu Zoo, Tomioka-oniisan (Saitama)

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:47.780
Their tails are flat and broad, a shape 
that is well-suited for swimming.

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:50.260
The tails are covered in scales,

00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:54.780
so they're an animal whose appearance is a bit 
different from how we imagine mammals.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:10:00.700
Their jaws, teeth, and muscles 
are so strong that they can gnaw

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:04.040
through a tree with a 15-centimeter 
diameter in only about ten minutes.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:05.780
It's said that when they go on land,

00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:09.400
they'll only go up to about 
twenty meters from the water.

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:12.170
They don't leave the shore much.

00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:17.530
Their formal name is the 
black-tailed prairie dog.

00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:43.140
Edogawa Zoo, Kawamura-oneesan (Tokyo)

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:20.880
The tip of their tail is black,
as if it was dipped in ink.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:22.860
Because they live underground,

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:26.950
they have sharp claws, and 
their ears and tails are small.

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:32.380
Their breeding season is in February and March,

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:35.490
and they'll fight each other 
very aggressively then.

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:39.460
Sometimes they'll harass their rivals

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:43.370
by closing up the tunnels a rival uses with dirt.

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:47.990
You are trying to build a home, too, Beaver-dono?

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:51.120
Indeed, I am attempting 
to make a dwelling myself.

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:58.380
The prairie dog builds burrows. 
They mainly live in prairie areas.

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:04.470
I like places with nice, clear views, 
so I wanted to make a home here.

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:08.190
But I dig and dig, and still it collapses.

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:13.170
Having this many holes probably makes 
it more unstable and dangerous.

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:15.820
Very worrisome.

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:21.360
Incredible! You know such things at a glance?

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:25.110
Please, will you share 
your knowledge with me?

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:29.350
We're here to look for trees. 
Do you mind if we cut them down first?

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:32.960
In that case, I'll lend you my assistance.

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:37.000
Which one would be good?

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:41.260
Hmm... It should be about this long...

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:44.810
But it would be a lot of work 
to carry wood back twice,

00:11:44.810 --> 00:11:46.010
so we should be precise as—

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:48.640
Let us not waste time! Charge!

00:11:57.310 --> 00:11:59.260
Wait! Wait!

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:00.530
Huh?

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:06.120
You can control where the tree falls 
by the way you cut it. For instance...

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:09.750
Gnaw, gnaw, gnaw, gnaw...

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:15.830
You start it like this, and then 
you carve out this side, and...

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:17.310
Gnaw, gnaw, gnaw...

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:24.930
I get it!

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:27.190
Beaver-san, that's superb!

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:29.890
I see. You use your teeth, yes?

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:33.400
I can fell one fast like this 
for a demonstration,

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:36.610
but I get anxious when it 
comes to the real thing...

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:45.840
I have prepared 100 more in the same way!

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:48.840
What say we adjust their lengths later?

00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:50.950
You caught on way too fast!

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:58.920
You're so fast, and the cuts are 
so clean. You have my respect!

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:04.080
My kind digs as a team, so I'm 
accustomed to following orders.

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:08.030
Beaver-dono, your intelligence is far 
more impressive. You have my respect!

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:18.300
I can't believe I got these materials so quickly.

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:21.070
It's thanks to all of you.

00:13:21.390 --> 00:13:26.490
The sturdiness, length, 
and width are all perfect.

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:31.240
This time, I'll use them carefully.

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:32.360
Great view: check!

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:33.380
Great sunlight: check!

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:37.460
And most importantly, it makes me 
want to dig! It's just perfect!

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:40.920
I must dig right now!

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:44.460
Is everything okay on your end?

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:46.010
I'll give it a try.

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:49.780
Materials, check. I'll start with the foundation,

00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:53.010
and keep the corners in mind...

00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:56.030
She can see everything she has to do, huh?

00:13:56.030 --> 00:13:58.400
Beaver's amazing.

00:13:58.400 --> 00:13:59.650
Now, then...

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:03.780
No, wait a minute. 
First, I need to check the lengths.

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:08.110
But once I cut something, I can't redo it...

00:14:10.310 --> 00:14:15.560
This might take me some time. 
You should go watch Prairie-san.

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:18.670
S-Sure. Don't overdo it, okay?

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:21.080
I wonder how Prairie's digging is going.

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:23.450
She might be finished already.

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:26.760
Wait, where is she?

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:28.010
Prai—

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:31.090
Prairie-san!

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:34.610
Help me! Help me!

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:35.560
Heave-ho, heave-ho...

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:40.120
You have my thanks. Before I knew it, 
I was buried alive again.

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:41.690
Are you okay?

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:44.570
What would you have done 
if we hadn't come by?

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:49.070
But I now understand this dirt! In I go!

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:53.570
Dig, dig, dig, dig, dig...

00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:57.800
Rock! I hit rock!

00:15:01.490 --> 00:15:03.080
Are you okay?

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:04.930
Much appreciated.

00:15:04.930 --> 00:15:08.050
Maybe you should dig a little slower...

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:09.420
Understood!

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:11.860
Prairie's pretty amazing, huh?

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:14.640
I wonder how Beaver-san's doing.

00:15:18.490 --> 00:15:21.730
It's in the same state as when we left!

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:26.680
When I think of how I absolutely 
can't fail this time,

00:15:26.680 --> 00:15:28.730
I get so scared that I can't cut them.

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:34.220
Kaban-chan, do you have any ideas?

00:15:34.810 --> 00:15:37.290
Let me think...

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:42.370
What if you made a miniature house 
first, as an experiment?

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:44.750
A miniature house?

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:48.100
To see how well the building will go 
when it's time for the real thing,

00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:50.770
you can make it at about this size first.

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:54.470
Good idea. I'll try it.

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:57.280
I wonder if Prairie's digging is going well.

00:15:57.280 --> 00:16:02.020
Help me! Help me!

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:01.300
Not again!

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:04.540
All right! Third time's the charm!

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:05.790
Wait, wait!

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:09.040
How about you plan <i>before</i> you start digging?

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:09.850
I see.

00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:12.030
Before I dig! I'll try it!

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:13.650
How's it going?

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:16.040
I thought I'd start with a model of the model...

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:18.080
You don't need to go that far!

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:22.020
I was working while thinking out 
my plan, or so I thought...

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:23.710
How did you get that idea?

00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:26.040
Could be better.

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:44.290
There, there.

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:46.150
Want some Japari buns?

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:49.240
Prairie-san, how did it go for you?

00:16:49.240 --> 00:16:53.340
I started about twenty burrows, 
but they all fell apart.

00:16:53.340 --> 00:16:55.330
Huh? That's so many!

00:16:55.330 --> 00:16:56.930
And you, Beaver-dono?

00:16:57.720 --> 00:17:01.390
I'm still at zero, even though 
I know how I can do it.

00:17:01.390 --> 00:17:04.250
You do? I'm jealous!

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:10.460
Wait...

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:16.330
Um, how about the two of you 
build something together?

00:17:16.330 --> 00:17:18.010
Together?

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:23.620
If you worked at my pace, it would 
take you so much longer. I'd feel bad.

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:27.900
And I'm sure I'd end up 
destroying Beaver-san's house.

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:30.560
How about if Prairie-san 
focuses on the building part,

00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:35.820
while Beaver-san makes the model 
and concentrates on giving directions?

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:40.110
We should try it! What 
do you two want to make?

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:44.280
I want a log house like this.

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:47.440
Holes. Holes! I want to dig holes!

00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:50.630
Then how about a room you 
can enter through a hole?

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:53.480
I need to live near water.

00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:55.000
How about over there?

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:58.580
Yeah! I'd like to dig a tunnel 
that reaches over there!

00:17:58.580 --> 00:17:59.730
What the heck?

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:02.310
Wow! I want to go through that tunnel!

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:05.470
Then I'll make a ladder so you can climb.

00:18:05.470 --> 00:18:07.100
Sounds fun!

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:09.190
This model is amazing!

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:14.230
It's good if the entrance is hidden. I want 
to make an entrance on this side, too.

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:16.740
I want a room underground!

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:20.190
I definitely like places with a good view.

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:22.700
Okay, we'll make it about three floors...

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:24.830
You can do that?

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:26.540
Wow!

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:33.340
Let's build it!

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:36.730
Okay, Beaver-san, we're ready 
for your instructions.

00:18:36.730 --> 00:18:41.900
L-Let's see... First, we need to dig a hole...

00:18:41.900 --> 00:18:44.140
Just what I was hoping for!

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:48.600
If you just dig like normal, 
it'll probably collapse, so go deeper.

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:53.020
Also, after you dig for a while, we'll 
reinforce it with wood, in a shape like this.

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:54.400
Like this?!

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:55.440
So fast!

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:57.940
Keep going a little lower.

00:18:57.940 --> 00:18:59.060
Roger!

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:01.610
I'd like you two to move the dirt.

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:02.620
Got it!

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:03.530
Okay!

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:05.330
Dig, dig, dig, dig...

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:09.540
Wow! It really isn't collapsing!

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:12.510
I made it to the other side!

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:16.950
Next, we'll start making columns.

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:18.250
Okay!

00:19:24.270 --> 00:19:27.610
<i>It's amazing how Prairie-san can 
just dig without hesitation.</i>

00:19:27.610 --> 00:19:30.310
<i>It's coming right along thanks to her.</i>

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:34.220
<i>Beaver-dono seems to know all there 
is to know about materials and dirt.</i>

00:19:34.220 --> 00:19:35.800
<i>It's amazing.</i>

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:39.400
<i>It feels great to be able to 
concentrate on digging.</i>

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:45.680
There's not much for us to do.

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:49.410
Yeah. Shall we clean up?

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:00.820
It's done!

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:06.570
The view is great.

00:20:06.780 --> 00:20:07.960
Whee!

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:11.390
This is great.

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:12.740
Hello!

00:20:14.370 --> 00:20:16.190
Hello again!

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:19.420
I'd love to have a place to lounge over here.

00:20:19.420 --> 00:20:20.920
That's a great idea.

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:22.710
How's this look?

00:20:22.710 --> 00:20:23.470
That was fast!

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:25.980
I see. Like this, yes?

00:20:25.980 --> 00:20:26.950
That was fast!

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:29.420
They make a perfect pair.

00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:30.550
Yeah, really!

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:40.770
Thanks to you two, we made a wonderful house.

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:43.720
We can finally live relaxing lives.

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:46.920
It's all thanks to Kaban-dono's suggestion.

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:48.100
Huh?

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:53.770
Oh, no. I'm so weak, I could barely help at all.

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:58.120
Maybe that's the kind of animal you are? 
One that's good at thinking.

00:20:58.120 --> 00:21:02.150
Yes! You are definitely a great animal!

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:04.950
Thanks!

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:06.820
Well, shall we go?

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:08.910
Wait. First...

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:14.760
Raccoon-san!

00:21:16.610 --> 00:21:20.940
My target already went down the mountain...

00:21:20.940 --> 00:21:23.760
See why I tell you to slow down?

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:25.580
Ta-da! Fancy a cup of tea?

00:21:25.580 --> 00:21:26.840
Fancy a song?

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:30.350
I am Crested Ibis...

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:29.820
Cafés...

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:32.370
...are great, aren't they?

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:33.350
I am searching for my friends.

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:37.250
No! My treasure calls for me!

00:21:37.250 --> 00:21:38.690
Treasure?

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:44.820
This is a great bed.

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:47.240
It was nice of them to make it.

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:49.210
They were interesting.

00:21:49.210 --> 00:21:51.320
Yes, they were a great pair.

00:21:51.320 --> 00:21:54.280
We're a great pair, too!

00:22:02.340 --> 00:22:04.040
Owie...

00:22:04.760 --> 00:22:07.970
Where did you come from?

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:43.240
PPP Preview!

00:23:43.240 --> 00:23:45.150
This week, we're learning about lions.

00:23:45.150 --> 00:23:46.970
Apparently, lions rest 
for twenty hours a day.

00:23:46.970 --> 00:23:48.170
Twenty hours?!

00:23:48.170 --> 00:23:51.890
But I think footage of us sleeping for 
twenty hours would sell well, too.

00:23:51.890 --> 00:23:53.250
Then let's just sleep forever.

00:23:53.250 --> 00:23:54.930
Ah, bliss.

00:23:54.930 --> 00:23:56.370
Next time: "Plains."
